---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
import { url } from '../lib/url';

const description =
  'Ways to support PNH India Foundation — share your story, volunteer, partner with us, or contribute to our work supporting PNH patients across India.';
---

<Base title="Support Us" description={description}>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Get involved"
    title="Support our work"
    lede="There are people living with undiagnosed or unsupported PNH in India right now. Every one of the things below helps us reach them."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="grid grid--2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Share your story</h3>
          <p>
            If you live with PNH or care for someone who does, your experience is
            the most valuable thing you can give. Patient stories reduce
            isolation for people who have just been diagnosed, and they carry
            weight in policy conversations that statistics do not.
          </p>
          <p>
            You choose how much to share and whether to be named. Nothing is
            published without your explicit consent, and you can withdraw it at
            any time.
          </p>
          <p><a href={url('/contact')}>Tell us your story →</a></p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>Volunteer</h3>
          <p>
            We are small, and skilled help goes a long way. We are particularly
            glad to hear from people who can offer translation into Indian
            languages, design, writing, social media, event organisation, or
            legal and accounting support.
          </p>
          <p>
            Peer supporters — patients and caregivers willing to talk to newly
            diagnosed families — are always needed.
          </p>
          <p><a href={url('/contact')}>Offer your time →</a></p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>For clinicians and hospitals</h3>
          <p>
            If you treat PNH patients, we would like to work with you. We can
            provide patient-facing material for your clinic and connect your
            patients with peer support.
          </p>
          <p>
            We are also mapping where PNH is being diagnosed and treated across
            India — a picture that does not currently exist and that patients
            badly need.
          </p>
          <p><a href={url('/contact')}>Work with us →</a></p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>Spread the word</h3>
          <p>
            Awareness is not a soft outcome for a rare disease — it is the
            mechanism by which people get diagnosed. Sharing our material with a
            doctor, a patient group, or your own network genuinely shortens
            somebody's diagnostic journey.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you know someone with unexplained haemolytic anaemia, suggest
            they ask about PNH testing.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Donations: information only, no payment gateway -->
  <section class="section section--muted">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="prose">
        <span class="eyebrow">Financial support</span>
        <h2>Contributing financially</h2>
        <p>
          Contributions fund the practical work: producing patient information,
          running peer support, reaching patients in places we currently do not,
          and awareness work with clinicians.
        </p>

        <div class="callout callout--brand">
          <h3>We are not accepting online donations yet</h3>
          <p>
            We would rather wait until our registration and reporting are fully
            in place than take money we cannot properly receipt and account for.
            If you would like to contribute, please
            <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>email us</a> and we will tell you
            exactly where things stand.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="todo-note">
          TODO (Foundation) — before publishing any bank or UPI details, confirm
          all of the following:
          <br />• The entity is registered (trust / society / Section 8 company)
          and has a bank account in the organisation's name.
          <br />• 12A registration is granted, if you intend to claim income tax
          exemption.
          <br />• 80G is granted, if you intend to tell donors their gift is tax
          deductible. Do not state or imply 80G before the certificate is issued.
          <br />• FCRA registration is in place <em>before</em> accepting any
          foreign contribution — including from NRIs holding foreign passports,
          and including small online payments. Accepting foreign funds without
          FCRA is a serious offence, so if you later add a payment gateway,
          restrict it to domestic payments until FCRA is granted.
          <br />• You have a donation receipt process and a privacy policy for
          donor data.
          <br /><br />
          Once confirmed, replace the callout above with the account details, and
          update `registration` in src/site.ts so the footer displays them.
        </div>

        <h3>What we will publish here</h3>
        <p>
          When we do open financial contributions, this page will carry the
          organisation's registration details, bank information, our 80G status,
          and a clear statement of how funds are used. We will publish annual
          accounts. You should expect that of any organisation asking you for
          money, including us.
        </p>

        <div class="btn-row">
          <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`} class="btn btn--primary">Email us about supporting</a>
          <a href={url('/about-us')} class="btn btn--secondary">About the Foundation</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
